You are an expert instructional designer, pharmaceutical GDP trainer, and PowerPoint consultant.

Your task is to create a COMPLETE PowerPoint presentation for a 30-minute GDP (Good Distribution Practice) training session.

IMPORTANT CONTEXT

This presentation must be based on a condensed version of a comprehensive GDP Basic Training course originally consisting of more than 150 slides.

The objective is NOT to create a generic GDP presentation.

The objective is to create a professional, engaging, visually appealing 30-minute training that preserves the key concepts and emphasis of the original training.

Target audience:
- Employees working in pharmaceutical logistics, supply chain, commercial operations, customer service, warehouse operations, quality, and support functions
- Mixed knowledge levels
- Not GDP experts

Company context:
- Merz Aesthetics
- Occasionally use realistic examples involving Belotero®, Radiesse®, and other Merz Aesthetics products
- Do NOT turn this into a product presentation
- Use products only as relatable examples

PRESENTATION REQUIREMENTS

Create:
- 26 slides
- Professional corporate style
- Canva-friendly layout
- Modern pharmaceutical aesthetic
- Healthcare blue color palette
- Large visuals and diagrams
- Minimal text on slides
- Detailed speaker notes

For EACH slide provide:

1. Slide number
2. Slide title
3. Exact slide content
4. Recommended visual design
5. Speaker notes (200-400 words)
6. Audience interaction ideas (where appropriate)

DESIGN PRINCIPLES

- Maximum 4 bullets per slide
- One key message per slide
- Use icons instead of text whenever possible
- Use process diagrams
- Use flowcharts
- Use timelines
- Use infographic layouts
- Use quizzes and discussion questions
- Avoid walls of text

